{"ts":"2026-07-31T06:28:25.155Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"66076e2c28cfb4fafc6fb839","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-vcs-5h6j"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Phase 5: the forge and the patch series"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Forgejo is right that project metadata belongs inside the repository, and the kernel's lore workflow is right that a change under review is a first-class object with a lifecycle. This phase makes both native: a patch series is an object kind, review state is a record, and a served repository exposes them so agents can propose, review and land changes without a second system holding the state."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Epic"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-31T06:28:25.155Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-31T06:28:25.155Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A patch series can be produced from a commit range, transferred, applied and re-derived byte-identically; review state is a record that merges per field so two reviewers never conflict; a served repository exposes refs, objects and series over the transport from Phase 3"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"dfdeb2b4a329e62e8aa6916d79206d8be7331fcaae2f7f923b60076b2b510313","message":""}
